--> find [path] [expression/criteria] [action]

1. by name or pattern 

--> case-sensitive search
	find /path/to/search -name "file.txt"

--> case-insensitive search
	find . -iname "file.txt"

--> wildcard matching
	find . -name "*.log"

2. By type (-type)

--> files only (f)
	find . -type f -name "*.txt"

--> directories only (d)
	find . -type d -name "config"

--> symbolic links (l)
	find . -type l

3. by size (-size)
	find /var -type f-size +100M   	// files larger than 100MB
	find /var -type f-size -10k   	// files smaller than 10KB
	find . -empty 			// empty files or directories
	
4. by modification time 
	find . -type f -mtime -7  	//modified in last 7 days
	find . -type f -mmin -60	//modified within the last 60 min

5. by permission and ownership
	find / -typr f -perm 777 	//files with exact permission 777
	find /home -user barsha		//files owned by specific user	




--> Performing actions on result 
1. Delete matched item directly
	find . -type f -name "*.txt" -delete

2. Execute a custom command per file 
	find . -type f -name "*.sh" -exec chmod +x {} \;		#Change permission on all target files
	find . -type f -name "*.conf" -exec grep -H "port" {} \; 	#Search for text inside matches (find + grep)

3.Combile with xargs (efficient for large lists)
	find . -type f -name "*.log" -print0 | xargs -0 rm -f   	#safely deletes all files ending in .log
